{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Read accounts and operational accounts often differ: order reviewers get reads, while staff changing status receive necessary write access."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I connected those separate accounts to QueryPie privileges. "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Advanced Privilege"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " lets different privileges use different accounts within one connection. I verified the actual account and audit evidence."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Preparing Read and Operator Accounts"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I created two accounts for the lab orders table: "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ep41_reader"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " received SELECT only; "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ep41_operator"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " received SELECT and UPDATE. Order 41001 started READY with amount 25000.00."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In the administrator view, I opened "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Databases → General → Configurations"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and enabled Advanced Privilege Setting, then opened Privilege Setting on the new "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "DB Privilege Account Lab"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " connection."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-account-mapping/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. Enabling Advanced Privilege Setting for per-privilege accounts.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. Enabling Advanced Privilege Setting for per-privilege accounts."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Read-Only uses ep41_reader; Read/Write uses ep41_operator"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Both Test Connection checks succeeded before saving, making the account split explicit within one connection."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-account-mapping/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. Different database accounts mapped to two QueryPie privileges.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. Different database accounts mapped to two QueryPie privileges."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Existing task-based database accounts can carry into QueryPie: administrators map accounts; users receive the appropriate QueryPie privileges."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Read Privileges Use the Reader Account"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Demo Developer first received Read-Only. The user view confirmed it, and Connect opened the web editor without entering a database password."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-account-mapping/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Lab connection and assigned Read-Only shown to the user.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Lab connection and assigned Read-Only shown to the user."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "While querying the order, I also checked "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "CURRENT_USER()"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", which shows MySQL’s authenticated account. It returned "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ep41_reader@%"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", with the prepared status and amount."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-account-mapping/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. Read-Only actually connects as ep41_reader.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. Read-Only actually connects as ep41_reader."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Checking the actual account, not just the privilege name, made the setting’s effect clear."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Operational Privileges Change the Account on Reconnection"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After disconnecting, the administrator changed the same user’s privilege to "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Read/Write"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Reconnecting and running the same SQL returned account "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ep41_operator@%"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-account-mapping/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. A new Read/Write connection uses the operator account.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. A new Read/Write connection uses the operator account."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The user chose the same connection, but privileges selected the account. No separate reader/operator passwords needed distribution."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I then changed order 41001’s status "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "from READY to CHECKED"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". UPDATE returned 1 Rows updated; a new read confirmed CHECKED and unchanged 25000.00."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-account-mapping/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. One order changed and verified using the operator account.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. One order changed and verified using the operator account."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Audits Retain Both User and Database Account"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In the administrator’s "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "DB Access History"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", the new connection showed Demo Developer, Read/Write, and DB User ep41_operator; the earlier one showed Read-Only/ep41_reader."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-account-mapping/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. User, QueryPie privilege, and actual database account in access history.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 7. User, QueryPie privilege, and actual database account in access history."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Query Audit"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " showed the UPDATE as Success, with user, time, Read/Write, and Web Editor route."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-account-mapping/08.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 8. UPDATE audit includes user, privileges, and success.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 8. UPDATE audit includes user, privileges, and success."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Further down were DB User, target table, and SQL, linking "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "who used which privilege and database account to execute which SQL"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " in one record."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-account-mapping/09.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 9. Operator account and SQL changing order 41001 in the same audit.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 9. Operator account and SQL changing order 41001 in the same audit."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Carrying Existing Account Separation into Access Management"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The company’s database-account model can map naturally to QueryPie users, retaining reader/operator separation while applying accounts to responsibilities."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Users work through assigned connections; administrators manage privileges and accounts together. Actual users and activity remain auditable, so "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "the purpose of separate accounts stays clear in both connections and work history."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This lab used QueryPie Community 11.6.7 and MySQL 8.0.42 with test users and orders."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reference: "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "link",
              "attrs": {
